body:
Slice 1 of 6 of #635, per the 2026-07-31 re-slicing after PR #647 (50 files / 19,228 added lines) was closed unmerged on reviewability. Each slice is budgeted at ~1,500 added semantic lines or less; the material is salvaged from #647's diff, not re-derived.

## What

- `ChunkMap::Flat | Segmented` on `InodeRecord` with decode-time invariants, each with a raw-byte negative case: `segment_count != segments.len()`, duplicate index, index gap, non-monotonic/overlapping byte spans, non-32-hex nonce, wrong-width key index;
- `seg:<nonce>:<epoch>:<index>` / `seggrp:` key helpers (fixed-width zero-padded index so byte-lexicographic order equals index order) and `SegmentRecord`;
- Flat stays a JSON array, byte-identical to today; legacy records decode -> encode byte-for-byte (every CAS in `metadata.rs` is `require(key, encode(prior))`, so any encoding drift turns every overwrite of every pre-existing object into a permanent `Conflict`);
- the record-shape paragraph of the living-architecture docs (docs-currency; the resolver and publication paragraphs land with the slices that land that behavior).

## Scope

`crates/core/src/metadata.rs` (shape + codec region and its co-located tests).

## Out of scope

The resolver and every consumer (slices 2-4); the chunk-id floor (slice 5); staged publication (slice 6).

## Salvage

Extract the shape/codec region and its inline tests from PR #647's diff.

## Acceptance

- legacy flat records round-trip byte-identically and CAS on pre-existing records still commits;
- each decode invariant has its raw-byte red case;
- a segmented root's encoded `inode:` value stays within the 100 KB value ceiling (measured in encoded bytes);
- `cargo xtask ci` green, including the prose gates (the docs paragraph lands here).

Part of #635 / #508 / epic #513.
